# MH fleet sizing for the Kind dev cluster (ADR-0039 §7 "On demand", §10).
#
# MH_BASELINE = B, the number of `baseline`-owned MHs infra/kind/scripts/deploy.sh
# keeps serving (it runs `mh.sh upgrade`, then tops up / drains to exactly B).
# THE ONE HOME of B: deploy.sh (write_mh_template) reads this file and renders
# it into the `mh-template` ConfigMap's `baseline` key, and everything else (mh.sh list
# `.baseline`, scripts/dev-web.sh, the env-test baseline checks) reads it back
# from there. Distinct from GC's per-meeting initial handler count.
#
# Constraints: 1 <= B and B + 1 <= K (K = the hostPort slot count, home
# crates/devloop-helper/src/ports.rs): an upgrade needs one free slot to start
# the new MH before draining the old, so deploy.sh fails `mh-no-free-slot`
# before touching anything when B + 1 > K. B < 2 breaks env-test 27's
# two-handler placement. Changing B is a redeploy (no cluster recreate).
#
# Deliberately NOT a configMapGenerator: no pod reads B (it is pool sizing, not
# MH config), and every ConfigMap in the environment-root render must be
# referenced by a pod template (dt-guard R-21, configmap_unreferenced). Format:
# exactly one `MH_BASELINE=<integer >= 1>` line; anything else fails deploy.
MH_BASELINE=2
